\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces One step of the two-level update. Top: a cheap coarse predictor produces a low-resolution global next state, prolonged to the fine grid as a context field $\bm  {C}_t$. Bottom: a shared fine network predicts each patch from its restricted state, halo, geometry, parameters, positional encoding $\bm  {e}_i$, and the coarse context. Patch predictions are blended by the partition of unity into $\bm  {S}_{t+1}$.\relax }}{2}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dataflow}{{2}{2}{One step of the two-level update. Top: a cheap coarse predictor produces a low-resolution global next state, prolonged to the fine grid as a context field $\bm C_t$. Bottom: a shared fine network predicts each patch from its restricted state, halo, geometry, parameters, positional encoding $\bm e_i$, and the coarse context. Patch predictions are blended by the partition of unity into $\bm S_{t+1}$.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
